`allow.hosts` contains `api.*.example.com`. A wildcard is permitted only as the whole first label (`*.example.com`) or as the whole entry (`*`); an interior wildcard has no agreed meaning across implementations. SPEC §4.4: a host is a lower-case DNS name, an IPv4 literal or `localhost`, with an optional single leading `*.` label, or the bare `*`; two implementations must not disagree about what a host entry names.
